{
  "requirement": "Each page has the same result fields as the originating tool. Text reads return\nsuccessive portions of text. Listings, outlines, and searches return successive\narrays of whole entries in their original order. Only a page with a successor\nincludes `next`.\n\nReusing a UUID returns the same page from the original snapshot, including the\nsame successor UUID if more remains. A malformed UUID, an unknown UUID, or a UUID\nfrom another conversation returns a tool error under\n{cite}`requirements.sdk.graph.agent-harness.tool_agent.isolation`.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The reviewed tests cover every obligation in `requirements.sdk.graph.validation-context.pages.behavior`. I read the paging implementation `Pages::prepare` and `Pages::get` in `pages.rs` only to see how the mechanism is shared. I derived the expected behavior from the requirement text.\n\n**Same result fields as the originating tool**\n- `search_pages_return_every_original_match_in_order` asserts `complete`, a valid `search_id`, and the exact `{node, excerpt, tag}` entries on every page.\n- `outline_continuations_keep_the_file_and_complete_ordered_items` asserts `node == \"code.rs#\"` on every page, plus `items`.\n- `listing_continuations_return_complete_paths_from_the_original_listing` reads `files` from each page.\n- `source_read_pages_retain_text_and_dependencies_without_another_read` asserts `node.selector` and `text` on each continuation page.\n\n**Text reads return successive portions**\n- `graph_read_pages_retain_the_prepared_snapshot_after_contents_change` concatenates the pages of a multibyte read and asserts the result equals the original text.\n- `source_read_pages_retain_text_and_dependencies_without_another_read` does the same for a source read.\n\n**Listings, outlines, and searches return whole entries in original order**\n- `listing_continuations_return_complete_paths_from_the_original_listing` compares the concatenated 2000 paths with the expected sequence.\n- `outline_continuations_keep_the_file_and_complete_ordered_items` checks all 401 items in order, with each `node` and `kind`.\n- `search_pages_return_every_original_match_in_order` checks all 350 matches against the original node and excerpt, in order, over more than one page.\n\n**Only a page with a successor includes `next`**\n- The loops in the listing, outline, and search tests end exactly when `next` is absent.\n- The graph read test asserts `next` is present only on the first of two pages.\n- The listing test asserts the first page has a `next`.\n\n**Reuse returns the same page from the original snapshot, with the same successor UUID**\n- `search_obligations_follow_delivery_and_keep_the_original_snapshot` rewrites the file, then fetches the continuation UUID twice, before and after finishing searches. It asserts the text is byte-identical, which includes the successor `next`. The search is large enough that this page has a successor.\n- The listing, outline, search, graph read, and source read tests all change or add files after preparing the first page. They assert the pages still reflect the original snapshot.\n- Reuse is only tested directly for the search pages. All page kinds share `Pages::get`, which clones the stored delivery. Replay is therefore structural, and a per-kind reuse test would add little.\n\n**Tool errors for bad UUIDs**\n- Malformed UUID: `outline_continuations_keep_the_file_and_complete_ordered_items` dispatches `get_next_page` with `\"invalid\"` and asserts an error.\n- Unknown UUID: the same test uses the all-zero UUID and asserts an error.\n- UUID from another conversation: `search_obligations_follow_delivery_and_keep_the_original_snapshot` asserts a peer session's `get_next_page` on the first session's `next` errors. `graph_page_ids_from_a_populated_peer_conversation_are_rejected` asserts the error result contains \"unknown page\" when a populated peer's UUID is used.\n\nThe cited `tool_agent.isolation` requirement is applied in the foreign-page tests. I found no gap, and there are no acknowledgments to account for.",
  "references": "1ac80069e6c37d2808f2a07935fa541926528e3931df8b3a2c423e0fed2a9800",
